ENTITY versioned_action_request_relationship;
  id : identifier;
  name : label;
  description : OPTIONAL text;
  relating_versioned_action_request : versioned_action_request;
  related_versioned_action_request : versioned_action_request;
END_ENTITY;



(*"versioned_action_request_relationship"
A *versioned_action_request_relationship* is a relationship between two
express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request]
objects.

[example]
Two express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request] objects may  be related if
they address similar problems.

[example]
A express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request] may be a version of a work request.
It might be related to a different version of the work request using a *versioned_action_request_relationship*.

*)


(*"versioned_action_request_relationship.id"
the
express_ref:[support_resource_schema.identifier]
that distinguishes the *versioned_action_request_relationship*.
*)


(*"versioned_action_request_relationship.name"
the
express_ref:[support_resource_schema.label]
by which the *versioned_action_request_relationship* is known.
*)


(*"versioned_action_request_relationship.description"
the
express_ref:[support_resource_schema.text]
that characterizes the *versioned_action_request_relationship*.
The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"versioned_action_request_relationship.relating_versioned_action_request"

one of the instances of
express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request]
that is a part of the relationship.


NOTE: The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize
this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.

*)


(*"versioned_action_request_relationship.related_versioned_action_request"

the other instance of
express_ref:[action_schema.versioned_action_request]
that is a part of the relationship.
If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.


NOTE: The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize
this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.

*)
